# Deploy

When the user says **deploy**, **redeploy**, **push to production**, or **deploy all changes**:

1. **Read** [docs/DEPLOY_INSTRUCTIONS.md](docs/DEPLOY_INSTRUCTIONS.md) (project root relative: `docs/DEPLOY_INSTRUCTIONS.md`).
2. **Execute** the steps in order in the project folder `c:\dev\TravelPlanner_v2`:
   - Ensure git is initialized and remote `origin` is `https://github.com/kimbersykes87-source/TravelPlanner.git`.
   - Run `git add -A`, then `git commit -m "..."` with a clear message (skip commit if nothing to commit).
   - Run `git branch -M feat/globe-loader`, then `git push -u origin feat/globe-loader --force`.
3. **Confirm** that the push succeeded; Cloudflare Pages will build and deploy from branch `feat/globe-loader`. Live site: https://travelplanner-ks.pages.dev

Use PowerShell on Windows; use `;` not `&&` when chaining commands. The project folder is the single source of truth; do not use `c:\dev\TravelPlanner` for deployment.
